class:: TempoRubato
summary:: Signed relative tempo change
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
Differentiates natural log BPM in time and multiplies by 100, then applies exponential smoothing. Invalid or low-confidence input breaks the derivative chain and lets the result decay toward zero.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: bpm
Control-rate tempo in BPM; nonpositive and nonfinite values are rejected as missing evidence.

argument:: confidence
Control-rate evidence weight, normally 0–1, default 1.

argument:: smoothing
Exponential derivative smoothing time in seconds, default 0.3; zero disables.

argument:: minConfidence
Minimum accepted confidence, default 0.1.

returns::
Approximate percent tempo change per second; positive means acceleration.

examples::
TempoRubato differentiates log tempo in physical time to measure instantaneous signed rate of tempo change (% acceleration or deceleration per second). In this example, it drives an expressive dynamic filter sweep: tempo accelerations open an auxiliary lowpass filter brighter, while decelerations darken the timbre. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the signed rubato rate in %/s.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var tempo = Tempo.kr(onset[1], tempoSmooth: 0.15);
        var rubato = TempoRubato.kr(tempo[0], tempo[1], smoothing: 0.25);
        var rubatoSmooth = rubato.lag(0.04);

        // Filter cutoff modulated by tempo acceleration
        var cutoff = rubatoSmooth.linlin(-15, 15, 400, 4500).clip(200, 8000);
        var filtered = LPF.ar(source, cutoff) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + filtered;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, rubato) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Tempo Rubato", ~mir2Bus, -20.0, 20.0, "%/s");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

